OL,3,APolice block Orange Order from
OL,4,Acontroversial parade route
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe police prevented an early morning
OL,7,Fattempt by the Orange Order to make a
OL,8,Fcontroversial parade down a road which
OL,9,Fhad previously been blocked by
OL,10,Fprotesters.
OL,12,FA group of men tried to march from
OL,13,FDrumcree Church down the
OL,14,Fmainly-nationalist Garvaghy Road in
OL,15,FPortadown in the early hours of Monday
OL,16,Fbut a line of police Land Rovers stood
OL,17,Fin the way.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1790580349
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,APolice block Orange Order from
OL,4,Acontroversial parade route
OL,5,
OL,6,FThey had been unable to make the
OL,7,Fpermitted parade on Sunday morning
OL,8,Fbecause protesters had gathered on the
OL,9,FGarvaghy Road. The stand-off continued
OL,10,Fthroughout Sunday, with the Orangemen
OL,11,Fwaiting at the church, around a mile
OL,12,Ffrom the road, for the go-ahead from
OL,13,Fpolice.
OL,15,FSinn Fein First Minister Michelle
OL,16,FO'Neill joined the protest, prompting
OL,17,FDemocratic Unionist Party (DUP) leader
OL,18,FGavin Robinson to accuse her of acting
OL,19,Funlawfully.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/39
